    Source: <repository URL>. Changes were made.

(Drop the final sentence if you made none.)

TWO THINGS THE LICENCE DOES NOT COVER, AND ONE THAT MATTERS MORE HERE THAN
USUAL:

  * It grants no trademark rights and no right to imply endorsement.
  * It grants no permission to do anything unlawful. This repository documents
    offensive security techniques. The licence permits you to COPY and ADAPT
    that documentation; it does not authorise you to USE the techniques against
    any system. That authorisation comes from the system's owner, in writing,
    and from nowhere else. See SECURITY.md.
  * The measurements in this repository are anonymised on purpose. If you adapt
    the material, you inherit that obligation as a matter of ethics if not of
    copyright: do not attempt to resolve a `com.vendor.*` pseudonym to a real
    vendor, and do not republish it if you do.


